            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac hemangioma presenting as atypical chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 44-year-old man presented with atypical chest pain and dyspnea. Investigation revealed the presence of a 15-mm rounded, well-vascularized left-ventricular mass. The mass was removed surgically and histopathologic evaluation identified a cardiac hemangioma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
